7. Default and Remedies

7.1. Events of Default

The Borrower shall be deemed to be in default under this Agreement if any of the following events occur:

* The Borrower fails to make any payment when due and payable;
* The Borrower fails to perform any obligation or covenant under this Agreement;
* The Borrower becomes insolvent or files for bankruptcy or insolvency proceedings;
* The Borrower makes any material misrepresentation or omission in any statement or representation made to the Lender or the Guarantor;
* The Borrower transfers or assigns this Agreement or any interest in the Loan without the prior written consent of the Lender.

7.2. Remedies

Upon the occurrence of an Event of Default, the Lender shall have the right to exercise one or more of the following remedies:

* Demand immediate payment of the outstanding principal amount and accrued interest;
* Accelerate the maturity date of the Loan;
* Take possession of the Collateral;
* Sell or otherwise dispose of the Collateral to satisfy the outstanding principal amount and accrued interest;
* Offset any amount owing to the Borrower against the outstanding principal amount and accrued interest;
* Take any other action permitted by law to protect its interests.

The Lender shall give written notice to the Borrower and the Guarantor of any exercise of a remedy under this Section, specifying the nature of the remedy and the amount of the outstanding principal amount and accrued interest.

