8. Security and Collateral

8.1. Security Interest

The Borrower hereby grants to the Lender a security interest in and to all of its right, title, and interest in and to the Collateral, including but not limited to the assets and properties of the Borrower, to secure the payment and performance of the Loan.

8.2. Collateral

The Collateral shall include, but not be limited to, the following:

* All of the Borrower's assets and properties, wherever located;
* All of the Borrower's rights, title, and interest in and to all intellectual property, including but not limited to patents, trademarks, copyrights, and trade secrets;
* All of the Borrower's rights, title, and interest in and to all contracts, agreements, and other obligations owed to the Borrower;
* All of the Borrower's accounts, chattel paper, and other financial assets.

8.3. Perfection of Security Interest

The Borrower shall take all actions necessary to perfect the security interest granted to the Lender in the Collateral, including but not limited to filing UCC-1 financing statements and recording deeds and other documents as required by law.

8.4. Maintenance of Collateral

The Borrower shall maintain the Collateral in good condition and shall not dispose of, sell, or transfer the Collateral without the prior written consent of the Lender.

8.5. Lender's Rights

The Lender shall have the right to take possession of and sell or otherwise dispose of the Collateral in the event of default by the Borrower.

