9. Events of Default

9.1. Failure to Make Payments

The occurrence of any of the following events shall constitute an event of default:

* The Borrower fails to make any payment when due under the Loan;
* The Borrower fails to pay any interest or fees when due under the Loan.

9.2. Breach of Covenants

The occurrence of any of the following events shall constitute an event of default:

* The Borrower fails to comply with any of the covenants and agreements set forth in this Agreement;
* The Borrower fails to maintain the Collateral in good condition.

9.3. Insolvency

The occurrence of any of the following events shall constitute an event of default:

* The Borrower becomes insolvent or bankrupt;
* The Borrower makes an assignment for the benefit of creditors.

9.4. Material Adverse Change

The occurrence of any of the following events shall constitute an event of default:

* A material adverse change occurs in the Borrower's business, financial condition, or operations;
* A material adverse change occurs in the value or condition of the Collateral.

9.5. Default Under Other Agreements

The occurrence of any of the following events shall constitute an event of default:

* The Borrower defaults under any other agreement or instrument to which it is a party;
* The Borrower defaults under any other agreement or instrument to which the Lender is a party.

9.6. Lender's Discretion

The Lender may, in its discretion, declare an event of default under this Agreement if it determines that any of the events described in this Section 9 have occurred.

